    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How much does a human virtual assistant cost vs an AI receptionist?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "A good real estate virtual assistant runs roughly $2,000-$3,500 per month fully loaded (wage plus recruiting, training, management time, and turnover risk), or $24,000-$42,000 in year one. A BirkyStudio AI receptionist is a one-time $550 setup for the voice line (client pays Vapi directly, about $30-$50/month for call usage) or $297 one-time for the WhatsApp text receptionist, with optional support at $29-$49/month. That's roughly $645-$1,618 in year one, a fraction of one month of a human VA."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Can an AI receptionist replace a human VA?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "For answering calls, qualifying leads, and handling routine inquiries, yes, an AI receptionist covers 24/7, never calls in sick, works in English and Spanish, and never quits. But a great human VA still beats AI on nuance, empathy, and relationship-heavy conversations where a client needs a warm human touch. The honest answer: an AI receptionist replaces the front-desk answering and lead-qualifying role, not the strategic, relationship-building work a top VA does."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What can't an AI receptionist do that a human VA can?",
