        "text": "An AI receptionist can't build the same personal rapport, read subtle emotional cues, negotiate complex deals, or handle judgment-heavy relationship conversations the way a skilled human VA can. It also can't do the broader admin work a VA does, scheduling, paperwork, transaction coordination, social media. If your business depends on deep, nuanced human relationships, keep a human for that. Use the AI for the 24/7 answering and qualifying that a human can't cover around the clock."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How much does BirkyStudio's AI receptionist cost?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "The AI Voice Receptionist is $550 one-time setup, with the client paying Vapi directly for call usage at roughly $30-$50/month, plus optional support at $49/month. The AI Text Receptionist for WhatsApp is $297 one-time with optional support at $29/month. There's no contract and no monthly platform fee, you own the setup. Compare that to a human VA at $2,000-$3,500/month."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Is an AI receptionist available 24/7?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Yes. A BirkyStudio AI receptionist answers calls and WhatsApp messages around the clock, 7 days a week, in English and Spanish, including at 2am, on weekends, and on holidays when a human VA is off the clock. It never calls in sick, never takes vacation, and never misses a lead because it stepped away."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Who should hire a human VA instead of an AI receptionist?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Hire a human VA if your business runs on deep, relationship-heavy conversations where a warm human touch and emotional nuance are the whole point, and you can afford $2,000-$3,500/month plus the recruiting and training overhead. Choose an AI receptionist if you need reliable 24/7 answering and lead qualification at a fraction of the cost, or if you want to cover the hours a human can't, most businesses end up using both."
      }
    }
  ]
});

const articleLD = JSON.stringify({
